AI/software support move with accepted and rejected suggestions, using relevant section concepts, evidence, or calculations.","explanation":"This direct-evidence item is used when no closed-response item adequately samples the objective. Score it with the section concepts and worked examples as the rubric.","difficulty":"medium","learning_objective_ids":["ail606-supplement-08-06-lo-03"]}]},"misconceptions":[{"id":"ail606_supplement_8_6_traffic_equals_success","pattern":"foot_traffic_as_showcase_goal","description":"Treating crowd size or foot traffic as the goal of a prototype showcase","trigger":"logistics optimize for milling visitors rather than evidence exchange","feedback":"Define the goal as visitors seeing theory-to-screen reasoning and presenters getting substantive questions, then design for that.","rail_action":"explain"},{"id":"ail606_supplement_8_6_no_focusing_prompt","pattern":"open_format_without_focusing_prompt","description":"Running an open house with no prompt that surfaces the README traceability matrix","trigger":"stations have no card or question directing visitors to the design reasoning","feedback":"Post a focusing prompt per station so the traceability matrix becomes the conversation, not an afterthought.","rail_action":"represent"},{"id":"ail606_supplement_8_6_unbalanced_stations","pattern":"unstaggered_starts_unbalanced_load","description":"Letting all visitors start together so popular stations crowd and others sit idle","trigger":"no rotation or staggered start, so visitor load is uneven across prototypes","feedback":"Use timed rotations with staggered start stations so every prototype is seen and no presenter is mobbed.","rail_action":"ask"}],"content_version":{"content_version":"b1d2d9d8c4bcc880db6973cb1587c5fe167fb1edce635019a6f654ba862ef2cf","algorithm":"sha256-mdx+meta+practice+misconceptions-v1","parts":["mdx","meta","practice","misconceptions"]}}